A commit is a saved snapshot of your staged changes.

git commit -m "message"	--- Save staged changes
git commit -am "message" --- Stage and commit modified tracked files
git log	 ----- View commit history
git log --oneline ---- Compact commit history
git show --- View latest commit details
git diff --- Compare unstaged changes
git diff --staged --- Compare staged changes
git commit --amend --- Modify the latest commit
